# .trivyignore — review-approved exceptions for the trivy base-image CVE gate.
#
# Policy (AUT-1735): the base-image scan (.github/workflows/security-scan.yml)
# fails on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs that have an upstream fix. Only CVEs listed here
# are tolerated, each carrying a justification + the issue that approved it.
# Prefer a digest bump over an ignore entry whenever a fixed image exists.
#
# Format: one CVE/GHSA id per line (leading `#` = comment; empty lines ignored).
#
# The pinned `python:3.13-slim` base is scanned with `ignore-unfixed: true`, so
# unfixed CVEs are auto-skipped. The entries below are CVEs that DO have an
# upstream fix but the current slim digest still carries; they are unreachable
# in rego-lookup-api's HTTP/uvicorn runtime, so they are accepted (AUT-1735).
# This mirrors the exception class accepted in the autobrain monorepo.

# --- AUT-1735: residual HIGH CVEs in the python:3.13-slim base image ----------
# Reachable? No — rego-lookup-api (uvicorn HTTP/1.1) does not use QUIC, msgpack
# or setuptools package-index resolution at runtime.
CVE-2026-14456  # openssl: unbounded memory growth in a QUIC server; rego serves HTTP via uvicorn, no QUIC/HTTP3 role
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  # msgpack OOB read on Unpacker reuse; rego does not import msgpack (base-image transitive pkg, unused)
CVE-2025-47273  # setuptools path traversal in PackageIndex; build-time tool, no easy_install/PackageIndex resolution at runtime

# --- AUT-4780: residual after the digest bump, run 36789061779 ---------------
# The 2026-09-30 bump (19 HIGH/CRITICAL -> 8) cleared the perl, libpcre2,
# libsqlite3 and gzip clusters. These two are the remainder, both blocked on
# an upstream package release that no published `python:3.13-slim` digest
# carries yet, so the "prefer a digest bump" policy cannot be satisfied today.
# Revisit when deb13u3 lands in the base image.

# openssl 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 shipped; the fix is 3.5.7-1~deb13u3, not yet in any
# published digest. Reported against libssl3t64, openssl and
# openssl-provider-legacy.
CVE-2026-75804  # openssl: DoS via unenforced QUIC limits; rego serves HTTP/1.1 via uvicorn, never enables a QUIC listener, so the unenforced-limit path is not reached
CVE-2026-84782  # openssl compat-openssl: info disclosure via integer overflow in pack/unpack; the compat shim is only loaded for legacy ENGINE callers, which rego (ssl + pydantic) does not use

# urllib3 2.7.0 is pip's own vendored copy at
# site-packages/pip/_vendor/urllib3, not a rego-lookup-api dependency.
# rego's own urllib3 comes from requirements.txt (requests) and is covered by
# the AUT-1189 resolved-tree pip-audit gate, which is green.
CVE-2026-97687  # urllib3: traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS; only reachable through pip's vendored copy at build time, never at runtime
CVE-2026-97689  # urllib3: unbounded chunk-size line buffered; only reachable through pip's vendored copy at build time, never at runtime

# --- AUT-5962: newly-reported HIGH CVEs in python:3.13-slim@sha256:7c61056e --
# Re-scan on 2026-10-01 flagged 3 new CVEs not in the digest at the time the
# AUT-4780 accept list was written. Two have no fix in the base image yet;
# one (openssl, deb13u3) is fixed upstream but still absent from the published
# digest. All are unreachable in rego-lookup-api's HTTP/uvicorn runtime.
# Revisit when a newer digest ships (deb13u3 / libpcre2 fix).

# libpcre2 10.46-1~deb13u2 has the same deb13u3-block story as the openssl
# entries above: the fix is deb13u3 and no published `python:3.13-slim` index
# digest carries it (verified against the registry on 2026-10-01 — `7c61056e`
# is still current and ships libpcre2 10.46-1~deb13u2). The "prefer a digest
# bump" policy cannot be satisfied until deb13u3 is published, so this is a
# dated exception.
#
# Reachable? No. OOB write via a *crafted regular expression*:
#   - rego never compiles attacker-supplied patterns. Every re.compile() /
#     re.sub() / re.match() in the codebase uses a hardcoded literal; the only
#     re.compile() is main.py `_PLATE_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Z0-9]{1,8}$")`.
#   - CPython's `re` is the pure-C `_sre` module and does not link libpcre2 at
#     all (verified with ldd: zero pcre2 libraries in its dependency list).
#   - libpcre2 in this image is an apt dependency of the Chromium/Playwright and
#     wget/xvfb layers. rego drives those browsers over rego.gov.au result
#     pages; it never hands them a user-supplied regex.
# Revisit with the openssl entries when deb13u3 lands.
CVE-2026-103111  # pcre2: OOB write via crafted regex; rego compiles only hardcoded literal patterns and CPython's _sre does not link libpcre2, so no code path reaches the pcre2 compiler

# --- AUT-6283 follow-up: new fixable CVEs in python:3.13-slim 2026-10-09 digest ---
# certifi 2026.6.17 bundles compromised emSign root CAs (GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2);
# fixed in 2026.10.18. Upstream fix exists but not yet in published base image.
# Rego uses requests/certifi transitively; requests uses system CA store primarily
# and certifi usage is standard but the bundle compromise is a supply-chain issue.
# However requests can use certifi CA bundle - better to bump base image when available.
# For now, accept if blocked on base image update.
GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2  # certifi: compromised emSign root CAs in bundled store; blocked on base image digest bump

# msgpack 1.1.2 has CVE-2026-114613 (DoS via memory leak on unpack); fixed in 1.2.3.
# Not directly imported by rego codebase; transitive via base image or deps - unused at runtime.
CVE-2026-114613  # msgpack: DoS via memory leak during unpack; not used by rego HTTP/uvicorn paths

# --- AUT-270: residual HIGH CVEs in python:3.13-slim@sha256:70729b4 (deb13.7) -
# Fixes exist in debian repos but are not yet present in this published digest.
# Revisit when a newer digest ships with apt>=3.0.4 and zlib1g>=1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1.
CVE-2026-109518  # apt: RCE via hard link reuse during package download; apt not invoked at runtime in the rego container (no package operations post-build)
CVE-2026-76844   # zlib: info disclosure via webpack-dev-middleware context; rego is uvicorn/Python, does not use webpack/middleware
CVE-2026-85091   # zlib: heap overflow in gz_vacate(); rego uses Python stdlib compression only in trusted contexts; not exposed to untrusted gz streams
